{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/control-reader-brief.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-2.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/control-reader-brief.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-2.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 5,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 650000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $550 billion and below $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 650000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $480 billion and below $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 480000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $420 billion and below $480 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 420000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 480000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $420 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 420000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Nvidia's total revenue in FY2028.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-24\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 650000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $600 billion and below $650 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 600000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 650000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $500 billion and below $600 billion, bracketing the cited $554 billion analyst estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 600000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $450 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i079\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-03\",\n    \"title\": \"Here's What a $25,000 Investment in Nvidia Could Be Worth if History Repeats Itself\",\n    \"passage\": \"In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Jensen Huang\",\n     \"what\": \"Blackwell and Vera Rubin sales\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$1 trillion\",\n     \"period\": \"March 2026 to end-2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e27 [party_statement; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e28 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, compared with trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e32 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA removed the AI Enterprise subscription requirement for Omniverse production use and allowed Omniverse-based products to be redistributed for free; the change was effective as of May 2026.\\n    Quote: The new terms remove that requirement entirely; anything built with Omniverse can also be redistributed under the same free terms, which is a substantive impact for ISVs and integrators who embed Omniverse applications inside their own products.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; storagereview.com; original source Mercedes-Benz ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] The Mercedes-Benz CLA, the first production deployment on NVIDIA's DRIVE platform, reached the US market in 2026.\\n    Quote: The first production deployment, the Mercedes-Benz CLA on the DRIVE platform, reached the US market this year.\",\n   \"- e34 [fact; SDxCentral, reporting the companies’ plan; original source Microsoft and MediaTek ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] Microsoft and MediaTek plan to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027.\\n    Quote: The pair plans to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027 .\",\n   \"- e35 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Google and Amazon, as reported by Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon claim their chips are better than NVIDIA's, although they use NVIDIA's products.\\n    Quote: The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e36 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Hock Tan ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Broadcom CEO Hock Tan says Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e45 [party_statement; Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais, as quoted by the outlet; original source Valve ; from gnews:c1658c3cc3b216fa2b0eaa54 2026-07-04] Valve engineer Pierre-Loup Griffais said Valve is working with Nvidia, AMD and Intel to expand SteamOS support across hardware.\\n    Quote: the company is working with AMD, Intel, and Nvidia to make the SteamOS experience better on a wider range of hardware.\",\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; xda-developers.com; original source Pierre-Loup Griffais ; from gnews:c1658c3cc3b216fa2b0eaa54 2026-07-04] The outlet reported that Griffais did not expect official SteamOS support for Nvidia GPUs before 2027.\\n    Quote: He doesn't expect anything before 2027, so Nvidia users have to wait, relying on Bazzite in the meantime.\",\n   \"- e47 [party_statement; BGR.com, reporting a statement by Josh Parker in an NVIDIA blog post; original source Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA head of corporate sustainability Josh Parker said AI compute demand driving data center construction was growing faster than almost any other infrastructure-investment category; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: AI workloads are not getting lighter. The compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other category of infrastructure investment.\",\n   \"- e50 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e51 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] Nvidia's revenue increased 1,033% from Q1 2024 through Q1 FY2027, which ended April 26.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\",\n   \"- e62 [fact; wccftech.com; original source US and European retailers ; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] US and European retailers are restocking NVIDIA’s GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB at prices starting at $329 and €333, respectively; the item gives no date for the retailers’ action.\\n    Quote: So as of right now, both US and European retailers are restocking the NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB with prices starting at $329 and €333, respectively.\",\n   \"- e63 [third_party_view; wccftech.com; original source wccftech.com 2026-07-05; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] wccftech.com reported that graphics card prices were continuing to rise as the DRAM crisis intensified in 2026; no price amount or comparison was given.\\n    Quote: As the DRAM crisis intensifies in 2026, graphics card prices continue to go up.\",\n   \"- e50 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project Nvidia revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e98, e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e71 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\\n    Quote: Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\",\n   \"- e72 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\\n    Quote: AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\",\n   \"- e73 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\",\n   \"- e74 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\\n    Quote: Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\",\n   \"- e88 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported calendar Q1 2026 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year.\",\n   \"- e89 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA's data center segment revenue was $75.2 billion in calendar Q1 2026, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e98 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 82% for the rest of 2026.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e50; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e99 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e50; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e100 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, 92% of total sales.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\",\n   \"- e101 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 92% year over year and 21% sequentially in fiscal 2027 Q1.\\n    Quote: Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.62 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, up 85% year over year; non-GAAP EPS was $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA guided to approximately $91 billion of total revenue in fiscal 2027 Q2, nearly 95% growth year over year.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e118; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e106 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by Danielle Liverance; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said agentic AI is generating value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.\\n    Quote: “Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.”\",\n   \"- e108 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom ASICs through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"- e109 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"- e110 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Micron ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% for next quarter.\\n    Quote: Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\",\n   \"- e111 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Unspecified estimates ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Unspecified estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n   \"- e116 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e147; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author estimates hyperscalers accounted for about 50% of NVIDIA's Q1 FY2027 data center revenue.\\n    Quote: About 50% of that data center number comes from hyperscalers\",\n   \"- e118 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 total revenue to $91.0 billion and non-GAAP gross margin to 75%.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion with non-GAAP gross margin holding at 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e119 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA networking revenue was $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year; the item does not specify the quarter in this sentence.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\",\n   \"- e120 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Amazon ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business is now worth multiple billions of dollars; no period is specified.\\n    Quote: Amazon has disclosed Trainium is now a multi-billion-dollar business\",\n   \"- e121 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon, Google, Microsoft, and Meta are building proprietary silicon, which the author says is intended to reduce costs and improve negotiating leverage against NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Amazon, Google, Microsoft, and Meta are all building proprietary silicon to cut costs and gain negotiating leverage over NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e122 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero; CFO Colette Kress described the future China market as close to $50 billion and said losing it would be material.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\",\n   \"- e123 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion of NVIDIA supply commitments and says they compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow; the period and definition of the commitments are not specified.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\",\n   \"- e124 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites NVIDIA data center revenue growth of 92%, gross margin of 75%, and quarterly free cash flow of $48.55 billion; the period for the growth and margin figures is not specified in this sentence.\\n    Quote: A company compounding data center revenue at 92% with 75% gross margins and $48.55 billion of quarterly free cash flow is a durable franchise.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e101; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e126 [fact; autonocion.com; original source Nvidia and Valar Atomics 2026-07-01; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] Nvidia and Valar Atomics announced an agreement to explore nuclear-powered AI systems, including a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah that would use no water from the local community; the factory is under study.\\n    Quote: Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”\",\n   \"- e127 [fact; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched its Querétaro AI Factory and neocloud offering, which it says is the first Blackwell-based neocloud in Mexico and Latin America.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\",\n   \"- e128 [party_statement; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said companies developing AI solutions have contracted all of the neocloud platform’s initial capacity.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\",\n   \"- e129 [party_statement; DCD reporter Cristina Cueto; original source Bleeding Edge 2026-07-06; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans to expand neocloud and AI Factory capacity in the coming months by adding Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\",\n   \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia plans to make up for the Rubin Ultra shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e139 [party_statement; Investing.com; original source Hon Hai management ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e140 [third_party_view; Monica J. White, How-To Geek; original source Monica J. White 2026-07-06; from gnews:349140be6b12bf5941071947 2026-07-06] How-To Geek author Monica J. White judged that AMD's RX 9070 XT is much cheaper than Nvidia's RTX 5070 Ti while offering similar performance, except for DLSS.\\n    Quote: The RX 9070 XT is much cheaper than the RTX 5070 Ti, but it offers similar performance, bar DLSS.\",\n   \"- e146 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis forecast NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above current Wall Street expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\",\n   \"- e147 [fact; tikr.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75 billion; the item does not specify the quarter.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter, the company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, with data center revenue alone hitting $75 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e155 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reportedly said NVIDIA changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet GPU to a dual-chiplet part the prior week, halving per-package compute because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\",\n   \"- e157 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months.\",\n   \"- e158 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] 80% of Chinese executives surveyed said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local suppliers take over; it says Beijing has urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\",\n   \"- e160 [fact; businesstimes.com.sg; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) over five years to build data centres and expand AI use across sectors.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\",\n   \"- e161 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of China’s core technologies, including chips.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\",\n   \"- e162 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s report says a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is positioned to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\",\n   \"- e108 [third_party_view; Danielle Liverance; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom ASICs through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e109 [party_statement; Danielle Liverance; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e116 [fact; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e147, e182; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e122 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, author Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero; CFO Colette Kress described the future China market as close to $50 billion and said losing it would be material.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e163 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in its upcoming production system; no deployment date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\",\n   \"- e164 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA and Hugging Face are integrating Isaac GR00T 1.7 and Isaac Teleop into Hugging Face’s LeRobot robotics library.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Hugging Face are collaborating to bring the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 open, reasoning vision language action (VLA) model for humanoid robots and the NVIDIA Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot — Hugging Face’s open source library for robotics\",\n   \"- e165 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA plans to integrate Cosmos 3 into Hugging Face’s LeRobot library soon.\\n    Quote: with NVIDIA Cosmos 3 , a frontier model for physical AI, planned soon.\",\n   \"- e166 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir announced it is combining its intelligence engine with Nvidia’s Nemotron models to deliver mission-focused AI for U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators.\\n    Quote: Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.\",\n   \"- e167 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com, recounting a CNBC interview; original source Alex Karp, CEO of Palantir 2026-07-01; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir CEO Alex Karp said Anthropic and OpenAI provide limited protection for clients’ intellectual property.\\n    Quote: In a CNBC interview, Karp said that the frontier AI model developers, Anthropic and OpenAI, have limited protections for their clients' intellectual property.\",\n   \"- e169 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\",\n   \"- e174 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SpaceX ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] SpaceX plans to use Nvidia as an initial hardware supplier for its orbital data centers; the item gives no date or amount.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is set to serve as an initial supplier of hardware for SpaceX's orbital data centers.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SpaceX ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] SpaceX plans for its first orbital data-center satellites, called AI1, to use Nvidia chips; the item gives no date or amount.\\n    Quote: SpaceX's first version of the satellites it plans to use as data centers in space is called AI1 and will use Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e182 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27, and CEO Jensen Huang described “the largest infrastructure expansion in human history”.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e183 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer engagement for MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading-customer forecasts above AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: CEO Lisa Su has said “customer engagement around MI450 Series and Helios is strengthening, with leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations.”\",\n   \"- e184 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year, and guided Q3 revenue to $16.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY, with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts 27% CAGR for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e108; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e186 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e188 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source id Software and Bethesda Softworks ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations would launch on July 7, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction and path tracing support.\\n    Quote: Later today, the DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations expansion launches with support for DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Ray Reconstruction, and path tracing.\",\n   \"- e189 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source Ubisoft ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced would launch on July 9, 2026, with DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Super Resolution and ray tracing support.\\n    Quote: On Thursday, Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced launches with DLSS Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution, and ray tracing.\",\n   \"- e190 [fact; NVIDIA; original source MADFINGER Games ; from gnews:2f1cb54b7a3da28d093523b6 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said Gray Zone Warfare had added its latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models for GeForce RTX GPUs.\\n    Quote: Now, the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models have been added to further enhance frame rates and image quality on GeForce RTX GPUs.\",\n   \"- e191 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source Three people with knowledge of the matter, as cited by Reuters 2026-07-06; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip, according to three people cited by Reuters.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek, the Hangzhou-based AI startup behind some of China's most advanced large language models, is developing its own custom AI chip, Reuters reported on Monday, citing three people with knowledge of the matter [1] . The chip is designed for inference — the phase where trained models generate responses to user queries — rather than for training new models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e195; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e192 [fact; mlq.ai; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] U.S. export controls bar Chinese companies from accessing the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory.\\n    Quote: U.S. export controls that bar access to the most advanced overseas foundries and restrict shipments of high-bandwidth memory — a component critical to inference chip performance [2].\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue and limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122, e198; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e195 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans, cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed sources cited by Reuters said DeepSeek is developing chips specifically for AI inference.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e191; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e196 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Unnamed Reuters sources ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Unnamed Reuters sources said DeepSeek's early-stage chip project has involved discussions over the past year with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters sources, DeepSeek's chip development project remains at an early stage. Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\",\n   \"- e197 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] DeepSeek increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months, without publicly posting the openings on general recruitment platforms.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months. The hiring process has been conducted discreetly, without publicly posting job openings on general recruitment platforms.\",\n   \"- e198 [third_party_view; Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and that DeepSeek is unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology; he said DeepSeek's development would not affect Nvidia.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e199 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.62 billion in fiscal 2027 Q1, up 85% year over year; non-GAAP EPS was $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; Danielle Liverance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e116, e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local suppliers take over; it says Beijing has urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg News; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of China’s core technologies, including chips.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e221; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e162 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence’s report says a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is positioned to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e222; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e200 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source LangChain ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, making the tuned harness available for enterprises to use.\\n    Quote: By tuning its Deep Agents harness specifically for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, it allows for high-performing agents that complete more tasks, run faster and give enterprises a fully open stack they can customize, own and run anywhere.\",\n   \"- e201 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Abridge, Amdocs, Box and EY ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents into their platforms, while EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents.\\n    Quote: Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents directly into their platforms and global systems integrator EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents, helping clients customize, evaluate and govern specialized agents across high-value workflows.\",\n   \"- e206 [fact; fool.com (John Bromels); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:79cc3f345545cdd3d37c0472 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported that revenue increased 74.6% in its most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter alone, Nvidia increased its revenue by 74.6%\",\n   \"- e210 [fact; Futuriom, relaying Bloomberg; original source Meta ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models.\\n    Quote: On July 1, the same day NVIDIA announced its new revenue-sharing model, Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business selling AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e214 [fact; CNBC; original source SambaNova 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova raised $1 billion in financing, led by General Atlantic with Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group participating; the round valued it at $11 billion.\\n    Quote: An AI chip startup has raised $1 billion in financing as investors continue to pour money into companies looking to challenge Nvidia .\",\n   \"- e215 [fact; CNBC; original source JPMorgan Chase 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova systems for on-prem inference in its enterprise AI workloads.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova's systems for \\\"on-prem inference in our demanding enterprise AI workloads.\\\"\",\n   \"- e216 [party_statement; SambaNova co-founder and CEO Rodrigo Liang, quoted by CNBC; original source Rodrigo Liang ; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova CEO Rodrigo Liang said the new capital would let the company accelerate deployments of racks customers want; he gave no deployment amount or date.\\n    Quote: \\\"We're scaling the business really, really fast, and so the capital allows us to really accelerate the deployments of the racks that customers really want,\\\" he said.\",\n   \"- e217 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg-tracked analysts ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg-tracked analysts project NVIDIA FY2027 profit of $228 billion and sales of $393 billion, up 90% and 82%, respectively; the profit estimate rose 13% over the prior three months.\\n    Quote: company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source puts NVIDIA's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\",\n   \"- e219 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings indicate Nvidia’s China market share is expected to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and domestic suppliers gain ground.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, citing Bloomberg News; original source China’s government-led initiative for the data-center buildout; Bloomberg News for the report that at least 80% of core technologies will be supplied domestically ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) over five years to build data centers, with at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, expected to come from domestic companies, according to Bloomberg News.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management. At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, citing the report; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg’s report says a global memory-chip shortage, particularly for high-bandwidth memory, is likely to cap Chinese AI firms’ growth, while ChangXin Memory Technologies is poised to benefit.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya reported that NVIDIA's sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capital-expenditure growth.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e225 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; qz.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] Nvidia's data center segment reported record revenue of $75.2 billion in FY2027's first quarter.\\n    Quote: while its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [party_statement; Tom’s Hardware; original source AMD ; from gnews:9fbd0f954b9cc2281da531d1 2026-07-08] AMD claimed its hardware would deliver 3.3x Vera’s performance for the projected output of a 100 kW rack; the item gives no statement date.\\n    Quote: AMD had some things to say about the Phoronix test, firing back with its own metrics of a 3.3x performance gain over Vera for the projected output of a 100 kW rack of its hardware.\",\n   \"- e228 [third_party_view; aibusiness.com, quoting Lian Jye Su; original source Lian Jye Su, analyst at Omdia ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Omdia analyst Lian Jye Su said Nvidia is facing challenges from Chinese vendors as humanoid robotics vendors rise in China.\\n    Quote: “The company is facing some challenges from Chinese vendors due to the rise of humanoid robotics vendors in China ,” Su noted.\",\n   \"- e229 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Qualcomm and Intel ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm recently entered robotics with Dragonwing IQ10, and Intel with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, challenging Nvidia’s position.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA reported that Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth rate of cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source BofA ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled Nvidia retaining roughly 65%–70% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\",\n   \"- e232 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net, reporting unnamed sources ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that Nvidia is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super cards in 2027 instead of launching the next-generation RTX 60 series.\\n    Quote: However, the news has been quite disappointing when it comes to the GeForce RTX 60 series cards. Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\",\n   \"- e233 [rumour; Notebookcheck.net, relaying Moore’s Law Is Dead; original source An unnamed Nvidia source, as relayed by Moore’s Law Is Dead ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed Nvidia source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that the RTX 60 series GPUs are not expected to come out in 2027.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027.\",\n   \"- e234 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck.net; original source Notebookcheck.net 2026-07-08; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reports that AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027, a potential competitive product launch for Nvidia.\\n    Quote: We have been hearing about the release timeline of the next-gen AMD and Nvidia GPUs for a while now. It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\",\n   \"- e235 [fact; Larsen & Toubro Vyoma; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix 2026-07-08; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma and Fortanix announced a partnership to offer sovereign AI infrastructure and secure workloads using NVIDIA Confidential Computing; the announcement gave no amount or timeline.\\n    Quote: Through this partnership, L&T Vyoma will provide sovereign AI infrastructure, including data centres, compute and networking, while Fortanix will secure the data and AI workloads in use by leveraging NVIDIA Confidential Computing.\",\n   \"- e27 [party_statement; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e252; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e258 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects Nvidia will hold 70%–75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e264 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta expects its MTIA 450 chip in early 2027 and MTIA 500 later in 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory. Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e267 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 to begin mass production of its AI5 chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e274 [rumour; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans to build European AI data centres with combined power capacity of 200 MW by the end of 2027, adding competing AI compute capacity.\\n    Quote: The company plans to build a network of AI data centres across Europe by the end of 2027, with a combined power capacity of 200 MW.\",\n   \"- e275 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of announced AI factory projects in Europe.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\",\n   \"- e163 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in its upcoming production system; no deployment date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e169 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house processors, increasing competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source puts NVIDIA's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e277; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e277 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein; original source Jeran Wittenstein 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding to competition with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition — not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips — is a major factor holding back Nvidia’s stock price.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e169, e291; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e291 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reported rumors that major NVIDIA clients were accelerating development of in-house AI chips, potentially increasing competition for NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: rumors of major clients accelerating their development of in-house artificial intelligence (AI) chips\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e295 [fact; quantumzeitgeist.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:b666d35e5247a8ddcc2d7c72 2026-07-10] Perplexity plans to integrate NVIDIA Vera CPUs into its upcoming production systems; no amount or date was given.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now planning to integrate Vera into its upcoming production systems, demonstrating confidence in its ability to enhance agent performance and overall system efficiency.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e297 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e194 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e157, e343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e327 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia said AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs during 2027–2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in August 2026 that AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs in 2027 to 2028 .\",\n   \"- e328 [third_party_view; io-fund.com; original source Yole Research ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Yole Research projected that more than 90% of servers would be CXL-capable by the end of calendar 2026, up from two-thirds in Q1 2025.\\n    Quote: Yole Research estimated that in Q1 2025, two-thirds of servers were CXL-capable , and projects this figure will rise to more than 90% by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"- e329 [party_statement; io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\",\n   \"- e331 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said Nvidia's Vera CPU could expand its addressable market beyond GPUs and create billions of dollars in additional revenue; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e332 [rumour; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (unnamed reports) ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports said Nvidia had begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow; no amount or period was specified.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e343 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Bloomberg survey ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e194; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia management expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth; no period or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\",\n   \"- e360 [fact; GuruFocus; original source Google ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, potentially expanding competition with Nvidia in AI chips.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\",\n   \"- e361 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity, indicating limited near-term openness to TPU adoption at that provider.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e362 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\",\n   \"- e383 [party_statement; Abhinav Raj, as reported by XDA Developers; original source AMD ; from gnews:6e27fc3ef50f99b180c6646a 2026-07-13] AMD has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 GPUs, with the rollout expected to extend into 2027.\\n    Quote: AMD, to its credit, has committed to bringing FSR 4.1 to RDNA 2 cards, but that rollout is expected to stretch into 2027, seven years after those GPUs launched and two full years behind the equivalent Nvidia moment.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports Morgan Stanley's forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; they added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025, while Google alone is forecast to add 6.8 GW in 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e391 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers are continuing to expand investment in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley says hyperscalers continue to expand their investments in proprietary silicon to improve total cost of ownership and reduce dependence on merchant GPU suppliers.\",\n   \"- e392 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that one GW of AI infrastructure costs $6 billion–$11 billion with Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks, versus roughly $19 billion with Nvidia GB300-based racks and $25 billion with Vera Rubin racks.\\n    Quote: Milk Road AI estimates that building one gigawatt of AI infrastructure using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks cost between $6 billion and $11 billion, compared with roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks. Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\",\n   \"- e28 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Justin Pope; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate Nvidia revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, compared with trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e401; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e401 [third_party_view; Justin Pope, The Motley Fool; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA total revenue of approximately $555 billion in FY2028, ending January 2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia will generate approximately $555 billion in revenue for the company's next fiscal year, ending January 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e404 [party_statement; Nokia, as reported by the outlet; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said it developed the first commercial AI-driven radio access network platform with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Nokia Oyj says it developed the first commercial artificial intelligence-driven radio access network platform together with Nvidia Corp to radically increase the amount of data operators can transmit using existing infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 6,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $550 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$550 billion to below $600 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $550 billion and less than $600 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 600000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$600 billion to below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $600 billion and less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 600000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2026\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"year\": \"