 $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e97; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e97 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management projected hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e125 [third_party_view; Allen Harris, citing Goldman Sachs; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026, rising to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with about $7.6 trillion cumulatively over 2026–2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031.\",\n   \"- e48 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The big four AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e97, e172, e177; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e172 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e177 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e186 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion, and Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e400 [third_party_view; Justin Pope, The Motley Fool; original source Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026; no amounts are specified.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\",\n   \"- e437 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon borrowed another $25 billion, a financing move the article connects with a selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 7,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Lowest\",\n    \"condition\": \"Below $850 billion\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 850000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Low\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $850 billion but below $950 billion\",\n    \"lo\": 850000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 950000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Middle\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $950 billion but below $1.05 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 950000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1050000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"High\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $1.05 trillion but below $1.15 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 1050000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1150000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Highest\",\n    \"condition\": \"At least $1.15 trillion\",\n    \"lo\": 1150000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Nvidia management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49, e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] Nvidia claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e177 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e321; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e321 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] Nvidia claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e96, e390; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; Rich Duprey; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports Morgan Stanley's forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; they added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025, while Google alone is forecast to add 6.8 GW in 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e437 [fact; ebc.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon borrowed another $25 billion, a financing move the article connects with a selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 8,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v9\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-24\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e204 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue above $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's most recent fiscal 2026 revenue topped $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year and well ahead of the $11.7 billion it posted in 2019.\",\n   \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\",\n   \"- e236 [fact; FEV Group; original source FEV Group and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices; no scale or completion date was given.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\",\n   \"- e237 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that memory makers have increased high-bandwidth memory chip prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply.\\n    Quote: For memory companies like Micron, the story is much simpler. They build high-bandwidth memory chips — specialized components designed to move data in and out of processors as fast as possible — which have been getting incrementally better for 20 years. Without the chips or the companies changing too much, the service they provide suddenly became very valuable — and since demand is growing faster t\",\n   \"- e238 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The article reports that the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then declined steadily.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e239 [third_party_view; Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said more GPU and accelerator players are entering the market and predicted that current market conditions would broadly persist absent an HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory-market entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market.\",\n   \"- e241 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Experts cited by barchart.com ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts cited by barchart.com say DeepSeek's chip is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, partly because China contributes less to Nvidia sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\",\n   \"- e247 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Edge Computing revenue was $6.4 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 29% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its Edge Computing revenue increased 29% YOY to $6.4 billion, supported by demand across gaming GPUs, autonomous driving, robotics, and AI-enabled edge devices.\",\n   \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\",\n   \"- e250 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported record data center segment revenue in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e251 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management guided to accelerating data center segment revenue growth in Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Moreover, management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e253 [third_party_view; Rick Munarriz; original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author says Nvidia's revenue growth accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\",\n   \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported 85% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal Q1, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity left to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e260 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon’s Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e261 [fact; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft announced its Maia 200 inference chip in January 2026, and the chip is now reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\\n    Quote: It announced Maia 200, a chip built for that work, in January 2026, and the chip is already reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\",\n   \"- e262 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft’s Maia 200 chip is planned to power OpenAI’s newest models and Microsoft AI products including Copilot.\\n    Quote: The chip will power OpenAI's newest models, along with Microsoft 's own AI products, such as Copilot.\",\n   \"- e263 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta’s MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation, and Meta plans to build three further MTIA generations over the next two years for generative AI models.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work. Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e265 [party_statement; qz.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI’s planned installation of its custom AI chips is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and continue through the end of 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e266 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference-chip design in April 2026 and plans production at TSMC’s Arizona plant and Samsung’s Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e268 [fact; gizmodo.com, as reported by Bruce Gil; original source Micron ; from gnews:fe9210b7b43c51e0939ecbbb 2026-07-09] Micron decided to wind down its Crucial consumer business brand to focus on data center demand; no date or amount was given.\\n    Quote: Micron even decided to wind down its consumer business brand , Crucial, to focus on data center demand.\",\n   \"- e269 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\",\n   \"- e270 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta's monthly sales rose to NT$385.19 billion in June 2026, more than doubling year over year; Quanta supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e205 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA FY2027 revenue of $392.7 billion.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e276; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e245 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Moreover, the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e250, e285, e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e248 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia forecast fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second-quarter guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue because of U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e254 [fact; Rick Munarriz; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported 85% year-over-year revenue growth in fiscal Q1, its strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244, e290, e292; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e269 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e284; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e276 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting Bloomberg-compiled data; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg-compiled projections put NVIDIA FY2027 sales at $393 billion, up 82% year over year.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e205; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e279 [fact; AWS; original source AWS 2026-07-10; from gnews:23d831f15e3a80d6b3ba60e6 2026-07-10] AWS introduced serverless customization on SageMaker AI for NVIDIA’s Nemotron 3 Nano and Super models.\\n    Quote: Now, SageMaker AI introduces serverless model customization for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 models, starting with Nemotron 3 Nano (30B total parameters, 3B active) and Nemotron 3 Super (120B total parameters, 12B active).\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e281 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis says NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: That figure seems high until you set it against what the company is actually delivering: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [party_statement; Trefis, relaying NVIDIA guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to upcoming-quarter revenue of $91 billion at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: For the upcoming quarter, the company guided revenue to a midpoint of $91.00 billion, signaling continued strong demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e248, e289, e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e283 [party_statement; Trefis, quoting NVIDIA management; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management said its Vera CPU opens a new total addressable market of $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Management sees its new Vera CPU opening a “brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA,” a market it has never addressed before.\",\n   \"- e284 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta plans to begin manufacturing its Iris custom AI processor in September 2026, after initial testing.\\n    Quote: Reuters said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e286 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e289 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e290 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The article cites NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75.0%.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e296 [third_party_view; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint reported that in June 2026 SK Hynix had 29% of the global DRAM market, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint .\",\n   \"- e298 [third_party_view; Thomas Richmond, quoting Kristina Partsinevelos; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said no additional HBM supply would arrive before late 2027, keeping the memory shortage and record-high prices in place until then.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e299 [fact; Thomas Richmond; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285, e304; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e300 [party_statement; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia estimates that supporting frontier AI models accounts for about 20% of its business; the item gives no period.\\n    Quote: To put some numbers behind that, Nvidia estimates about 20% of its business comes from supporting frontier AI models built by companies like OpenAI and Anthropic.\",\n   \"- e301 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen estimates Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range; the item gives no period or explicit unit for the range.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\",\n   \"- e302 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing; no amount or period was specified.\\n    Quote: Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing\",\n   \"- e303 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that recent cloud computing deals were signed at premium prices; no counterparties, amounts, or dates were specified.\\n    Quote: recent cloud computing deals have been signed at premium prices.\",\n   \"- e304 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, in the quarter; this was its third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e299; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e306 [party_statement; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia expects its Vera CPU line to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of the fiscal year; the article date places that year in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also highlighted a new growth driver: its Vera CPU line, which the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year, a notable push into a market historically dominated by Intel and AMD.\",\n   \"- e307 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia and Valar Atomics ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia and Valar Atomics have a deal to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah to support AI computing and reduce water use; no capacity or completion date was specified.\\n    Quote: Beyond the CPU expansion, Nvidia has been striking new partnerships, including a deal with Valar Atomics to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah aimed at reducing water use for AI computing.\",\n   \"- e308 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Perplexity chose to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks; no deployment date or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: AI startup Perplexity has also chosen to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks.\",\n   \"- e309 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Mark Zuckerberg ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg commented that progress in AI agents was slower than expected; the article gives no specific measure or period.\\n    Quote: Comments from Meta’s Mark Zuckerberg about slower-than-expected progress in AI agents have also added caution to the broader AI narrative.\",\n   \"- e310 [third_party_view; TIKR.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Bank of America views the recent semiconductor-sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than evidence that AI demand is fading.\\n    Quote: Still, firms like Bank of America view the recent semiconductor sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than a sign that AI demand is fading, keeping names like Nvidia stock in focus for investors watching this space closely.\",\n   \"- e311 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley estimated that AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\",\n   \"- e281 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis says NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: That figure seems high until you set it against what the company is actually delivering: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244, e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e314 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held more than 90% of the AI-chip training market in 2025.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025.\",\n   \"- e315 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held 60%–75% of the AI-chip inference market in 2025, with custom silicon competition reducing its share.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch\",\n   \"- e317 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that Anthropic's Claude was running on more than one million Amazon Trainium2 chips as of March 2026.\\n    Quote: with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\",\n   \"- e318 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95%, depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\",\n   \"- e319 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia revenue increased 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\",\n   \"- e322 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI in late 2026 and into 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\",\n   \"- e330 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] The article reports that Nvidia’s server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\",\n   \"- e333 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292, e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported fiscal Q1 2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e335 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Nvidia management forecast approximately $91 billion in total revenue for fiscal Q2 2027, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293, e345; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e336 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Wall Street consensus, as reported by barchart.com ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street expected Nvidia's fiscal 2027 total revenue to exceed $300 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\",\n   \"- e337 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported quarterly revenue of about $35 billion, up 198% year over year and a record.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e338 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst), citing Counterpoint Research; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research estimated SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\",\n   \"- e339 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix and NVIDIA ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix and NVIDIA signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e340 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e347 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expanded partnerships with Alphabet and Marvell.\\n    Quote: expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL)\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and net income of $58.32 billion, up 211% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase, while net income jumped 211% YOY to $58.32 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e281, e363; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Nvidia Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027 first-quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286, e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e285 [fact; 247wallst.com, summarizing NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e299, e334, e373, e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China, and NVIDIA reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e249, e368, e380; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e292 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254, e333, e367; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282, e335, e366, e381; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e305 [fact; TIKR.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year, in the quarter; the exact period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245, e365; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e344 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333, e364, e372, e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e345 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e335, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e349 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive chief Xinzhou Wu estimated that autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of all miles driven, without specifying a measurement period.\\n    Quote: Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\",\n   \"- e350 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia hopes to earn a share of ecosystem revenue for each autonomously driven mile, which he described as a potential trillion-dollar opportunity; he gave no timing.\\n    Quote: We hope that we can get a percentage of the revenue that the ecosystem can get from every mile that is driven autonomously in the future. This is where the trillion-dollar opportunity can come from.\",\n   \"- e351 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla is ahead of other companies in L2++ advanced driver-assistance technology and that competitors are trying to catch up.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody. He had a division a long time ago and he has stuck to the vision for a long time to develop and test the technology among a massive fleet. Nobody would argue that Elon is ahead of everybody in the ADAS market and everybody is playing a catch-up game, essentially.\",\n   \"- e352 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu forecast that Level 4 self-driving could become a mainstream experience in less than five years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\",\n   \"- e353 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense; he did not specify timing or the size of any increase.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e354 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia offers two Hyperion 10 sensor configurations: a base version with 10 cameras and three radars and no lidar, and a high-end version with 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars for Level 4 driving.\\n    Quote: In Hyperion 10, for example, we really offer two versions. One is a base, which is mostly cameras: 10 cameras, three radars, no lidar. It’s a very cost-effective way to build a L2++ ADAS kind of vehicle. And on the other hand, for the high end, is what we call the Hyperion High: we provide the sensor set required, which has, I think, 14 cameras, three lidars, and seven radars to have enough sensor\",\n   \"- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and in vehicles from some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\",\n   \"- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia and Uber were working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years; he did not give a specific date.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 driving; he did not specify a measurement date.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e358 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said Nvidia has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\",\n   \"- e363 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e364 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e344; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e365 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported record data center revenue of $75 billion for FY2027 Q1, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e305; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e366 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia management forecast FY2027 Q2 revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e293; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e367 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year; Data Center revenue was $75.246 billion and networking revenue grew 199%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, with Data Center at $75.246 billion and networking alone up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e292, e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e368 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 guidance assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA leans on scale and CUDA gravity, but assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance, a headwind Broadcom does not carry to the same degree.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e369 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion, up 143% year over year, as well as total revenue of $22.187 billion, up 47.9%.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s Q2 FY2026 revenue hit $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, with AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion growing 143%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e379; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e370 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com; original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom guided to Q3 FY2026 AI revenue of $16.0 billion, about 54% of total sales.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s Q3 earnings report lands September 8, and management has already telegraphed $16.0 billion in AI revenue, roughly 54% of total sales.\",\n   \"- e371 [third_party_view; 247Wallst.com; original source 247Wallst.com 2026-07-13; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom’s adjusted EBITDA margin was 69%, according to the article, supporting the author’s comparison of its ASIC business with NVIDIA’s GPU business.\\n    Quote: Broadcom is compounding a narrow, high-margin ASIC business with an adjusted EBITDA margin of 69%.\",\n   \"- e372 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion, +85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e344, e377; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e373 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center at $75.25 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e374 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang characterized the AI factory buildout as “the largest infrastructure expansion in human history.”\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang called the AI factory buildout “the largest infrastructure expansion in human history.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e382; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e375 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argu