 \"- e417 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027, attributed to InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Quote: Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e418 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: unusual for a company guiding to $91 billion in Q2 revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e409; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e419 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.23% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e420 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking was the sleeper hit at $14.8 billion (+199% YoY), driven by InfiniBand, Spectrum-X, and NVLink.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e423 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91 billion, assuming zero China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e424 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e285; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e425 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported that consensus analyst estimates for Nvidia increased 13.7% over the three months before 2026-07-14; the estimate measure and fiscal period are not specified.\\n    Quote: Analysts have been steadily raising their estimates for Nvidia. Over the past three months, the Zacks Consensus Estimate for the company has increased 13.7%.\",\n   \"- e426 [third_party_view; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Zacks ; from gnews:f10cd8ddb00105698ac294cf 2026-07-14] Zacks reported expected Nvidia earnings of $9.10 per share for the fiscal year ending January 2027, unchanged from the year-ago reported figure.\\n    Quote: For the fiscal year ending January 2027, this maker of graphics chips for gaming and artificial intelligence is expected to earn $9.10 per share, which is unchanged compared with the year-ago reported number.\",\n   \"- e427 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities, as reported from documents and sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] U.S. authorities permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra to purchase Nvidia H200 chips; a Kingsoft subsidiary was cleared to use some AMD chips.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips, while Zhuhai Hengqin Yunxiang Zhisheng Network Technology, a subsidiary of cloud computing company Kingsoft, has ‌been cleared to use some ⁠AMD chips that rival the H200, according to the documents and the sources.\",\n   \"- e428 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources familiar with the matter 2026-07-14; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain Nvidia H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: However, some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\",\n   \"- e429 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1, 2026, to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\",\n   \"- e430 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, planned to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e431 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42’s first stage of its Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e432 [party_statement; Rest of World; original source Peng Xiao, G42 CEO ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said Stargate’s machines would be mostly Nvidia despite G42’s efforts to spread orders among suppliers.\\n    Quote: G42 has spent months trying to spread its orders among several suppliers, yet the machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\",\n   \"- e434 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Reuters ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters said Chinese technology firms had more than 2 million Nvidia H200 chips on order about six months before 2026-07-14, exceeding Nvidia's available inventory at the time.\\n    Quote: But even with those domestic production initiatives, the Chinese hunger for AI silicon is so deep that six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\",\n   \"- e438 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI published an RFI seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its CJIS Division, including Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs; the RFI does not commit the FBI to a procurement.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1].\",\n   \"- e439 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024, while potential contract awards reached $91.8 billion, up from $4.6 billion in 2024.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase. Potential contract awards ballooned to $91.8 billion, up 1,912% from 2024's $4.6 billion [2].\",\n   \"- e440 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Airlangga Hartarto ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia’s Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 GW, in addition to roughly 580 MW already operating; no project period was specified.\\n    Quote: Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said investors are planning data center projects with a combined capacity of about 1.3 gigawatts (GW), on top of the roughly 580 megawatts (MW) currently in operation.\",\n   \"- e444 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported on July 14 that NVIDIA had more than halved its authorised Asian AI-chip customer list after creating a new whitelist to prevent chips reaching China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new “white list” of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e445 [rumour; Reuters; original source Three unnamed people familiar with the matter, cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] Three people familiar with the matter told the Financial Times that NVIDIA intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\",\n   \"- e446 [fact; Reuters; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May to curb advanced AI-chip transfers to overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concern that Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia despite US restrictions.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia’s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\",\n   \"- e447 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures after pressure from Washington, with staff now visiting customers’ data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers’ data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e448 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources cited by the Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is providing oversight and political backing for the compliance checks.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
