diture of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i232\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\", \"passage\": \"2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Alphabet / Google\", \"what\": \"capital expenditure guidance\", \"how_much\": \"up to $190bn\", \"period\": \"2026\", \"status\": \"forecast (guidance)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i233\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\", \"passage\": \"Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Google Cloud\", \"what\": \"revenue growth and backlog\", \"how_much\": \"revenue +63%; backlog nearly doubled to over $460bn\", \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\", \"status\": \"happened\"}}, {\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}] EVIDENCE COUNT 10\nCONTROL 7 RULER {\"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Below $700 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\", \"lo\": null, \"hi\": 700000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\", \"lo\": 700000000000.0, \"hi\": 800000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\", \"lo\": 800000000000.0, \"hi\": 900000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 900000000000.0, \"hi\": 1000000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\", \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\", \"lo\": 1000000000000.0, \"hi\": null}]} JUDGED {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027?\", \"looks_at\": \"Combined data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027\", \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\", \"year\": \"2027\", \"kind\": \"theme\"} ITEMS [{\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i090\", \"day\": \"2026-07-04\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\", \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\", \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\", \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i143\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\", \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"unnamed estimates\", \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\", \"how_much\": \"about half\", \"period\": \"2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i161\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 \\u2014 Is Micron the new Nvidia?\", \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\", \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\", \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\", \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\", \"condition\": \"could reach\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}] EVIDENCE COUNT 11\nCONTROL 8 RULER {\"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\", \"rungs\": [{\"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 500000000000.0, \"hi\": null}, {\"label\": \"Bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\", \"lo\": 400000000000.0, \"hi\": 500000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Neutral\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\", \"lo\": 350000000000.0, \"hi\": 400000000000.0}, {\"label\": \"Bearish\", \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\", \"lo\": 300000000000.0, \"hi\": 350000000000.0}, {\"label